  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "planner_runs: never relaunch a decision Planner for a held task whose hold fingerprint is unchanged since its last launch",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label E9.\n\nWhat exists and why neither field works as the fingerprint (luna-inbox .orchestrator/runs/planner_runs.json, read\n2026-10-01): records carry packet_hash (set at launch, orchestrator/planner_runs.py:1440) and state_version\n(planner_runs.py:946-954, a hash over every child's status, hold_reason, merged_into AND max event seq). luna has 161\ndistinct launches; 23 were a second launch on the same held task 3-8 min after the first, all on the exited_early\nretry path (record status gave_up, attempts 2, two 'launches'), and in every one BOTH packet_hash and\nstate_version had changed because routine pipeline events bump the seq. The 17 'same packet_hash' cases in the\nusage analysis are sections of one grouped launch (gap 0 s), not relaunches. So E9 needs a dedicated hold\nfingerprint that ignores event seq and pipeline timestamps.\n\nFacts (main 355583c):\n- planner_runs.py:168-210 decision_points() yields (goal, 'held', '<task>:<held_at>') for each held execute child\n  without a live fix round, unless _blocked() (135-138) finds a running/claimed/exited_ok/gave_up record.\n- reconcile() (674-751) turns a dead running record into exited_ok when _condition_resolved() (588-616) holds,\n  else exited_early (attempts 1, not blocking: retried next tick) and gave_up at 2.\n- Launch bookkeeping: legacy run() -> _record_running() (284-306); routed run_group() (1254-1447) updates\n  records to running at 1432-1444 and the goal guard at 1445.\n\nChange:\n1. hold_fingerprint(task) -> 12-hex sha256 over a canonical JSON of: id, status, hold_reason, resume_hint,\n   (result or {}).get('commit'), and sorted (id, status, merged_into) of every task whose\n   constraints.fix_round_for or constraints.respec_for is this id or whose depends_on contains it. No pipeline, no\n   events, no timestamps.\n2. Store hold_fingerprint on the record (and its launches entry) whenever a 'held' point launches, in both\n   _record_running and run_group's running update.\n3. decision_points(): for a held candidate, if any record of kind 'held' whose payload_key starts with\n   '<task id>:' has status exited_early, gave_up or exited_ok and a stored hold_fingerprint equal to the task's\n   current one, do not yield it. failed_launch, infra_failure and skipped records never suppress (the Planner never\n   ran). Send notify.notify_once(goal, 'hold_unchanged:<task>:<fp>', ...) once so the human sees the stall.\n4. Leave state_version, goal_launches guards, scouts_done and closable unchanged.\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE; update to the new contract):\n- tests/test_planner_runs.py::test_reconcile_exited_ok_exited_early_gave_up_and_gave_up_blocks_redecision\n  (~473-510) asserts the held key is yielded again right after exited_early ('not blocked yet', ~496) with the\n  hold unchanged. Under E9 it is not; change the hold (e.g. a new resume_hint) before that assertion, or assert it\n  is suppressed, keeping the gave_up-at-2 and notify checks.\n- tests/test_planner_runs.py::test_same_state_version_never_relaunches (~1255) and the FailedLaunch class\n  (~321-410, scouts_done) must pass unchanged.\n- Run tests/test_planner_runs.py, tests/test_planner_runs_packets.py and tests/test_planner_runs_routing.py.\n\nNote: E12 also edits planner_runs.py and depends on this task.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_planner_runs.py::test_unchanged_hold_fingerprint_never_relaunches: passes: after a decision Planner for a held task exits early (reconcile -> exited_early), decision_points() does not yield that task and tick() launches nothing while the hold is unchanged, even after unrelated pipeline/event writes change state_version; once the task's hold_reason or resume_hint changes, or a fix-round child appears, it is yielded again",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
